    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1107">

                <pb facs="0927" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/446.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-17T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1912—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inform all deserving Americans who may wish to return to the United States and
                    have no other means to do so that the <hi rendition="#italic">Buford</hi> will
                    touch at Manzanillo on or about May 22, San Bias May 23, and Mazatlan May 24. It
                    is desired to give the trip northward as great publicity as possible, and in
                    time to inform all Americans who need assistance and transportation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
